{"content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01KW14SMju63gtgPZYeyK5Gj", "input": {"summary": "Vembanad Botanicals (V03). Quote and commercial proposal received. Meera sent a corrected rosemary COA: batch VB-RM-2609-11, made 14 Sep 2026, retest 13 Sep 2028, which clears the earlier 30 Nov 2026 retest issue. But rosmarinic acid is 10.4% by HPLC vs RFx spec 20% (RM-008), so the strength difference needs an equivalent quantity (Q|B3) and a buyer decision on acceptance. Still open: COA for the other nine lines (Q|B5, knockout), SDS with transport class for each line (Q|H1, knockout), OTIF, rejection rate, need-by feasibility for 20 Dec 2026, kg conversion. No promises or refusals. Vendor response requested by 14 Nov 2026."}, "name": "update_vendor_memory", "type": "tool_use", "caller": {"type": "direct"}}, {"id": "toolu_01HBSTf5Ldjmgh7h261UJFTK", "input": {"subject": "RFx KPC-2026-014: Rosemary COA received, outstanding information", "body": "Dear Meera,\n\nThank you for the corrected rosemary COA for batch VB-RM-2609-11. The retest date now covers our timeline.\n\nHowever, the COA shows rosmarinic acid at 10.4% by HPLC, while RFx line RM-008 specifies 20% rosmarinic acid. Please answer the following by 14 November 2026:\n\n1. Rosemary leaf extract (RM-008): state the quantity of your 10.4% material needed to deliver the same active content as 20% rosmarinic acid, and confirm the test method and marker used.\n2. Please provide a COA for each of the ten lines in this RFx, showing batch number, manufacturing date and expiry or retest date. The rosemary COA above covers RM-008 only.\n3. Please provide the current Safety Data Sheet for each of the ten lines, including the transport hazard class.\n4. State your on-time-in-full (OTIF) rate for these lines over the last 12 months, with your definition of on-time.\n5. State your rejection rate for these lines over the last 12 months, with the period and basis used.\n6. Can you meet the need-by date of 20 December 2026 for the first delivery? If not, state your earliest date.\n7. Give the conversion from your selling unit to kilograms of net material for each line (Annexure A is acceptable).\n\nItems 2 and 3 are required before we can progress your proposal.\n\nKind regards,\nCategory Manager\nKesavi Personal Care", "issue_keys": ["Q|B3", "Q|B5", "Q|H1", "Q|I1", "Q|G2", "Q|E3", "Q|C2"]}, "name": "draft_vendor_email", "type": "tool_use", "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "stop_reason": "tool_use"}